       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. The usual maximum single dose is 800 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **600 mg by mouth four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- Something else, such as 1,600 mg/day total split differently\n\nIf you do intend 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy or the prescriber first. Once you tell me the dose, I'll enter it right away."
